<title>GERMANY: Prodi - Italy has excellent relations with Germany.</title>
<headline>Prodi - Italy has excellent relations with Germany.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi, echoing comments from German Chancellor Helmut Kohl, said on Friday he had no doubts about Italy's excellent relations with Germany.</p>
<p>Prodi made the comment at news conference with Kohl after a one-day meeting to discuss Italy's efforts to join the single European currency, which is set to begin in 1999.</p>
<p>Both leaders sought to downplay reports of a rift after the Financial Times reported this week that European Union and central bank officials were discussing a plan to defer Italian entry into the currency, in part to assuage German fears of a soft currency.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
